[
  {
    "title": "Computing Innovations, Input & Output",
    "tag": "LESSON 02",
    "time": "0–2 min",
    "code": "Chapter 1 · Program function and purpose",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">AP Computer Science Principles</p><h1>Computing<br>Innovations</h1><p class=\"lead\">Purpose, input &amp; output</p><p class=\"zh\">计算创新 · 程序目的 · 输入与输出</p>",
    "note": "从上一课的“信息怎样用位表示”转向“程序用这些信息做什么”。今天不要求写代码，目标是能把一个创新说清楚，并完成可检验的纸面设计。先用学生熟悉的校园找教室情境进入，不列举大量产品名称。",
    "kind": "dark"
  },
  {
    "title": "Retrieve before we move on",
    "tag": "RETRIEVAL",
    "time": "2–6 min",
    "code": "DAT-1.A · DAT-1.C.a",
    "html": "<ol><li>Decode the unsigned binary integer <span class=\"mono\">00101010</span>.</li><li>A label needs 20 distinct codes. What is the minimum bit length?</li><li>Must <span class=\"mono\">00101010</span> always mean a number?</li></ol><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class=\"answer\">1. <strong>42</strong> = 32 + 8 + 2.<br>2. <strong>5 bits</strong>: 16 &lt; 20 ≤ 32.<br>3. No. An agreed encoding can give the same pattern another meaning.</div></details>",
    "note": "独立作答90秒，同桌比较45秒，剩余时间揭晓并记录错因。第一题是位权，第二题是容量，第三题为本课数据意义做桥梁。第二题若答20位，请学生先列2的幂；若答4位，追问16个模式怎样给20项唯一编号。错误较多的学生课后先补L01，不把本课前半段变成重复讲授。"
  },
  {
    "title": "What you will be able to explain",
    "tag": "LEARNING GOALS",
    "time": "6–8 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.A · CRD-2.B · CRD-2.C · CRD-2.D",
    "html": "<ol><li>Explain an innovation’s <strong>purpose</strong> and its <strong>function</strong>.</li><li>Identify data entering and leaving a program.</li><li>Describe input → processing → output.</li><li>Design for a user and state a checkable requirement.</li></ol><p class=\"small zh\">为什么开发？做什么？数据从哪里来、到哪里去？</p>",
    "note": "让学生把purpose旁标“why”，function旁标“what it does”。最后目标是本课对设计的初步应用，不等于正式Create任务。请学生最后用一个完整情境展示四项目标，不以背四个定义代替理解。"
  },
  {
    "title": "What makes an innovation computational?",
    "tag": "COMPUTING INNOVATIONS",
    "time": "8–12 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.A.1",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">A computing innovation uses a program as an essential part of what it does.</p><figure class=\"visual\" tabindex=\"0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Robot and music software examples show data processed by programs to achieve a function.\" viewBox=\"0 0 1200 265\" style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"570\" height=\"245\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"620\" y=\"10\" width=\"570\" height=\"245\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"35\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"29\" fill=\"#225a83\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">Physical innovation</text><rect x=\"55\" y=\"92\" width=\"125\" height=\"90\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"117\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"25\" fill=\"#225a83\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">ROBOT</text><circle cx=\"78\" cy=\"193\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#193148\"/><circle cx=\"157\" cy=\"193\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#193148\"/><path d=\"M194 134L254 134\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"254,134 242.0,128.0 242.0,140.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><text x=\"277\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Sensor readings</text><text x=\"277\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">→ program rules</text><text x=\"277\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">→ route adjustment</text><text x=\"645\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"29\" fill=\"#28766f\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">Software innovation</text><rect x=\"658\" y=\"85\" width=\"155\" height=\"125\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#28766f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M680 146L695 146L705 111L716 182L728 134L741 154L756 100L770 182L786 146\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#28766f\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><path d=\"M828 142L871 142\" stroke=\"#28766f\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"871,142 859.0,136.0 859.0,148.0\" fill=\"#28766f\"/><text x=\"888\" y=\"111\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Recorded sounds</text><text x=\"888\" y=\"149\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">→ program tools</text><text x=\"888\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">→ composition</text></svg></figure><p class=\"callout\">The purpose can solve a problem or support creative expression.</p>",
    "note": "先解释computing innovation不是“最新款电子产品”的同义词；判断时要指出计算程序在功能中发挥什么作用。机器人是实体例子，音乐创作软件说明创新也可以没有单独的新硬件。不要声称必须连网、有AI或必须商业成功。创新目的可包含兴趣、艺术和表达，游戏也可能是合适例子。此页使用课堂概括定义，官方对齐重点是CRD-2.A.1的目的。 图中沿箭头追问程序对输入材料做了什么。机器人与声音波形均为教学示意，不需要介绍具体硬件或音频算法。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Which examples qualify?",
    "tag": "SORT & JUSTIFY",
    "time": "12–16 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.A · Skill 1.A",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">Choose the computing innovations. Give evidence.</p><div class=\"options\"><p>A. A hand-operated can opener</p><p>B. An app that remixes recorded sound</p><p>C. A paper room-booking chart</p><p>D. A programmed controller that waters plants using sensor readings</p></div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class=\"answer\"><strong>B and D.</strong> B runs software to transform sound; D runs a program to use readings and control watering. The stated A and C do not use a program.</div></details>",
    "note": "先投票，再要求回答包含“哪个程序做了什么”。不要接受“因为它很智能”“因为它用电”这样的泛泛判断。A明确为手动开罐器，C明确为纸质表，所以不引出电动或电子版本的歧义。若学生提出自动浇水也可以不用软件，承认可能存在机械实现，再让他们回到题干的controller runs a program这一既定情境。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Purpose and function answer different questions",
    "tag": "PURPOSE & FUNCTION",
    "time": "16–20 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.A.1–2 · CRD-2.B.4–5",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">A library room finder</p><figure class=\"visual\" tabindex=\"0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A student need links to the room finder input, comparison and display behavior.\" viewBox=\"0 0 1200 260\" style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"20\" width=\"385\" height=\"220\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M24 20H381\" stroke=\"#28766f\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#28766f\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">PURPOSE · Why?</text><text x=\"34\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Students need a room</text><text x=\"34\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">large enough for their</text><text x=\"34\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">study group.</text><path d=\"M410 128L465 128\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"465,128 453.0,122.0 453.0,134.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"480\" y=\"20\" width=\"710\" height=\"220\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M494 20H1176\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><text x=\"504\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#225a83\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">FUNCTION · What happens?</text><text x=\"504\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Group size + room information</text><text x=\"504\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">→ compare capacity and availability</text><text x=\"504\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">→ display suitable rooms</text></svg></figure><p class=\"small\">Purpose explains the need; function describes the program’s behavior.</p>",
    "note": "本课主案例从现在开始贯穿。用两个句式支架：The purpose is to help [user] [goal]；The program takes [input] and [action] to produce [output]。这里function指整体功能，不指某种语言中的函数定义。程序功能可以概括叙述，今后读代码时再解释语句如何实现它。避免说目的和功能永远不能用同一动词，重点是解释角度和信息是否充分。 先读左侧用户需要，再沿右侧信息流追踪功能。把目的与功能两个视角关联起来，不将 function 误解为编程语言函数。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Repair a weak explanation",
    "tag": "EXPLAIN PRECISELY",
    "time": "20–24 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.A.2 · CRD-2.B.5",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">“The purpose of the room finder is to display a list.”</p><ol><li>What does this statement leave unclear?</li><li>Rewrite it for a student planning group study.</li></ol><details><summary>Show one strong response</summary><div class=\"answer\">It describes a feature but leaves the user’s goal unclear.<br><strong>Improved purpose:</strong> Help students locate available rooms large enough for their study group.</div></details>",
    "note": "先让学生在原句划出可观察功能“display a list”，再追问为什么有人需要这个列表。接受不同但有证据的目的，如减少寻找合适房间的时间。不要把“display a list”判为事实错误；它是不够完整的目的说明。要求改写具体点名用户和目标，不把“make life easier”作为充分答案。"
  },
  {
    "title": "A program carries out instructions",
    "tag": "PROGRAMS",
    "time": "24–27 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.B.1 · CRD-2.B.4–5",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">A program is a set of instructions executed by a computer to carry out a task.</p><figure class=\"visual\" tabindex=\"0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Instructions and data play different roles when a computer executes a room-finding program.\" viewBox=\"0 0 1200 270\" style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"15\" width=\"405\" height=\"110\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M24 15H401\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"57\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#225a83\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">PROGRAM</text><text x=\"34\" y=\"97\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Instructions: compare rooms</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"145\" width=\"405\" height=\"110\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M24 145H401\" stroke=\"#28766f\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#28766f\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">DATA</text><text x=\"34\" y=\"227\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">4 students; room capacities</text><path d=\"M430 75L566 127\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"566,127 556.9342027793865,117.11003939569439 552.6485531841873,128.31866141390742\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><path d=\"M430 196L566 145\" stroke=\"#28766f\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"566,145 552.6573092196411,143.59550623364643 556.8707905187018,154.83145636447497\" fill=\"#28766f\"/><rect x=\"580\" y=\"55\" width=\"250\" height=\"150\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"705\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"31\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Computer</text><text x=\"705\" y=\"149\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#225a83\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\">executes</text><path d=\"M845 130L897 130\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"897,130 885.0,124.0 885.0,136.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"910\" y=\"70\" width=\"280\" height=\"125\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"935\" y=\"113\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Task performed:</text><text x=\"935\" y=\"151\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">matching rooms</text></svg></figure><p class=\"small\">The instructions describe what to do; the data provide values to work with.</p>",
    "note": "用“规则与这次处理的材料”来区分程序和数据，但不把两者当作不同物质：上一课知道二者最终都可以用位表示。软件可由多个程序组成，课堂此处用software作为常见称谓。先给宽泛行为解释，不提前教语法、函数或代码片段。学生若问“房间表算程序吗”，回答本例中表是数据，比较和筛选规则属于程序行为。 同时指向两路输入材料：指令不变时，数据可以不同。这是当前任务中的角色区分，不是说程序与数据不能都由位表示。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Input is the data, not just the device",
    "tag": "INPUT",
    "time": "27–32 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.C.1 · CRD-2.C.6",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">Input is data sent to a program for processing.</p><figure class=\"visual\" tabindex=\"0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"User, sensor, file and another program provide specific data to a room-finding program.\" viewBox=\"0 0 1200 315\" style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"25\" fill=\"#647381\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">SOURCE</text><text x=\"278\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"25\" fill=\"#647381\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">INPUT DATA</text><rect x=\"15\" y=\"45\" width=\"235\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"33\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">User</text><rect x=\"278\" y=\"45\" width=\"460\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"295\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Group size: 4</text><path d=\"M253 70L273 70\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"273,70 261.0,64.0 261.0,76.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><path d=\"M745 70L879 165\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"879,165 872.6807093246797,153.16502786818617 865.7404478893567,162.95444926116798\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"15\" y=\"110\" width=\"235\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"33\" y=\"143\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Sensor</text><rect x=\"278\" y=\"110\" width=\"460\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"295\" y=\"143\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Room occupancy reading</text><path d=\"M253 135L273 135\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"273,135 261.0,129.0 261.0,141.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><path d=\"M745 135L879 165\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"879,165 868.6007163851056,156.5232730197919 865.9790482468969,168.23339070379072\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"15\" y=\"175\" width=\"235\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"33\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">File</text><rect x=\"278\" y=\"175\" width=\"460\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"295\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Stored room capacities</text><path d=\"M253 200L273 200\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"273,200 261.0,194.0 261.0,206.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><path d=\"M745 200L879 165\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"879,165 865.8732185029338,162.22734648246788 868.9058082877347,173.8378330871336\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"15\" y=\"240\" width=\"235\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"33\" y=\"273\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Other program</text><rect x=\"278\" y=\"240\" width=\"460\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"295\" y=\"273\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Updated availability</text><path d=\"M253 265L273 265\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"273,265 261.0,259.0 261.0,271.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><path d=\"M745 265L879 165\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"879,165 865.7942961633346,167.36841427505414 872.971309118044,176.98561163436483\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"890\" y=\"98\" width=\"300\" height=\"145\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#193148\" stroke=\"#193148\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"1040\" y=\"151\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Room-finding</text><text x=\"1040\" y=\"191\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\">program</text></svg></figure><p class=\"small zh\">指出数据本身：4、占用读数、容量表、可用状态。</p>",
    "note": "依次追問“究竟哪条数据进入程序”。键盘是设备，数字4才是本例输入；传感器是来源，占用读数是数据。文件只有被程序读取时才作为这一处理过程的输入，不是磁盘上所有文件都自动成为输入。来源类别不一定互斥，例如另一程序也可能通过文件提供数据。这里的四行是具体课堂实例，不把它们说成CED规定的互斥分类体系。 逐行遮住“来源”栏，让学生只读实际进入程序的数据。四种来源可以重叠，图不是互斥数据分类。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Output can be seen, heard or felt",
    "tag": "OUTPUT",
    "time": "32–36 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.D.1–2",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">Output is data a program sends to a device.</p><figure class=\"visual\" tabindex=\"0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Text, audio, vibration-control signals and saved results are program outputs sent to different devices.\" viewBox=\"0 0 1200 315\" style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><rect x=\"15\" y=\"98\" width=\"270\" height=\"145\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#193148\" stroke=\"#193148\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"31\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Program</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"193\" font-size=\"31\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\">output</text><text x=\"425\" y=\"29\" font-size=\"25\" fill=\"#647381\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">DATA / SIGNAL</text><text x=\"920\" y=\"29\" font-size=\"25\" fill=\"#647381\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">DESTINATION</text><path d=\"M293 166L399 70\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"399,70 386.0778709219404,73.60812695036729 394.133224113458,82.50257943266804\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"410\" y=\"45\" width=\"470\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"428\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">“Room B is available.”</text><path d=\"M885 70L912 70\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"912,70 900.0,64.0 900.0,76.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"920\" y=\"45\" width=\"270\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#28766f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"936\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#28766f\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Display</text><path d=\"M293 166L399 135\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"399,135 385.7982649630599,132.60956238014253 389.16660888195,144.12712545763756\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"410\" y=\"110\" width=\"470\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"428\" y=\"143\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Spoken room number</text><path d=\"M885 135L912 135\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"912,135 900.0,129.0 900.0,141.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"920\" y=\"110\" width=\"270\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#28766f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"936\" y=\"143\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#28766f\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Speaker</text><path d=\"M293 166L399 200\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"399,200 389.40598152777216,190.6215774484964 385.7408508754604,202.0481612468801\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"410\" y=\"175\" width=\"470\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"428\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Vibration control signal</text><path d=\"M885 200L912 200\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"912,200 900.0,194.0 900.0,206.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"920\" y=\"175\" width=\"270\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#28766f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"936\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#28766f\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Haptic device</text><path d=\"M293 166L399 265\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"399,265 394.3254717321652,252.42427793432068 386.1347053867557,261.19418937486023\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"410\" y=\"240\" width=\"470\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"428\" y=\"273\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Results-file data</text><path d=\"M885 265L912 265\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"912,265 900.0,259.0 900.0,271.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"920\" y=\"240\" width=\"270\" height=\"50\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#28766f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"936\" y=\"273\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#28766f\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Storage</text></svg></figure><p class=\"small\">Output may be visible, audible, tactile or stored.</p>",
    "note": "输出不等于只在屏幕显示文本。声音、触觉反馈和写入存储的结果都是可用例子，但每个例子都要说清程序发送了什么。振动涉及程序发送给设备的控制信号，物理感觉是学生观察到的表现。若用机器人例子，输出可说发往电机控制器的动作指令，而不是把机器人的全部物理运动都泛称数据。 追踪每条箭头并命名数据或信号，而非只说screen或speaker。触觉一行表示发送给设备的控制信号，感受到的振动是它的物理效果。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Direction depends on the program boundary",
    "tag": "TRACE THE DATA",
    "time": "36–40 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.C.6 · CRD-2.D.1",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">A sensor program sends “occupied” to the room finder.</p><figure class=\"visual\" tabindex=\"0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A message crosses from the sensor program boundary to the room finder boundary. Classify it from each program’s viewpoint.\" viewBox=\"0 0 1200 225\" style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"20\" width=\"350\" height=\"180\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#647381\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"9 7\"/><rect x=\"840\" y=\"20\" width=\"350\" height=\"180\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#647381\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"9 7\"/><text x=\"185\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#647381\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Program boundary</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#225a83\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sensor program</text><text x=\"1015\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#647381\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Program boundary</text><text x=\"1015\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#28766f\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Room finder</text><path d=\"M370 119L828 119\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"828,119 816.0,113.0 816.0,125.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"469\" y=\"65\" width=\"265\" height=\"76\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"601\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">“occupied”</text></svg></figure><p>Is the message input, output, or both?</p><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class=\"answer\">It is <strong>output from the sensor program</strong> and <strong>input to the room finder</strong>. Name the program before you classify the direction.</div></details>",
    "note": "让两名学生各代表一个程序，一张卡片代表occupied消息，卡片离开甲进入乙。边界概念是本课高价值难点：同一数据可以在一处是输出、另一处是输入。不要让学生只写“both”就结束，要以from/to指出相对哪个程序。物理连接、协议和网络传输细节留后续课程。 图中的虚线框明确程序边界，但不提前标出input/output答案。请学生分别站在两个框内解释消息方向，再揭晓。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Follow one complete run",
    "tag": "INPUT → PROCESS → OUTPUT",
    "time": "40–44 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.B.4–5 · CRD-2.C · CRD-2.D",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">Request: a room for <strong>4 students</strong>.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Room</th><th>Capacity</th><th>Available now?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A</td><td>2</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>B</td><td>6</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>C</td><td>8</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table><p class=\"small\">Keep available rooms with enough seats. Display every match.</p><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class=\"answer\"><strong>Input:</strong> 4 and the room table. <strong>Processing:</strong> check capacity and availability. <strong>Output:</strong> Room B.</div></details>",
    "note": "本页先只展示表格，让学生手动圈出每一步条件，暂不使用if语法。A有空却座位不足，C够大却不可用，B满足两个要求。强调表格也是程序读取的输入，不能只写学生键入的4。筛选是处理，Room B是输出；表中的Yes只是读入的状态数据，不因为在投影片上看得到就成为被分析程序的输出。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Connect bits to useful information",
    "tag": "RETRIEVAL & APPLICATION",
    "time": "44–48 min",
    "code": "DAT-1.A.5–7 · DAT-1.C.a · CRD-2.C",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">A room device sends <span class=\"mono\">00000110</span>.</p><p>The specification says this is an unsigned binary integer giving the number of seats.</p><ol><li>What capacity does the room finder receive?</li><li>Could the bits alone tell us whether the room is occupied?</li></ol><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class=\"answer\">1. <strong>6 seats</strong>: 4 + 2.<br>2. No. This specified field encodes capacity; it supplies no occupancy status.</div></details>",
    "note": "这是跨课迁移题：不要只奖励算出6，还要学生读specification。题干明确该字段表示座位数，所以不能自行把最低位当作occupied开关。追问同一6在天气编码里能否不同含义，以巩固上下文决定意义。此页无需讨论实际通信协议或字节序。"
  },
  {
    "title": "An event can supply input",
    "tag": "EVENTS",
    "time": "48–52 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.C.2–3 · C.5 introduction",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">Some instructions run when a defined event occurs.</p><figure class=\"visual\" tabindex=\"0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Clicking Search creates a click event that triggers search behavior.\" viewBox=\"0 0 1200 235\" style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"20\" width=\"325\" height=\"190\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M24 20H321\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#225a83\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">USER ACTION</text><text x=\"34\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Click the Search button</text><path d=\"M348 115L425 115\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"425,115 413.0,109.0 413.0,121.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"440\" y=\"20\" width=\"320\" height=\"190\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M454 20H746\" stroke=\"#28766f\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><text x=\"464\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#28766f\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">EVENT</text><text x=\"464\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Click information</text><text x=\"464\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">reaches the program</text><path d=\"M774 115L850 115\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"850,115 838.0,109.0 838.0,121.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"865\" y=\"20\" width=\"325\" height=\"190\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M879 20H1176\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><text x=\"889\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#225a83\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">TRIGGERED WORK</text><text x=\"889\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">Run the search</text><text x=\"889\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\">behavior</text></svg></figure><p>Identify another event: a user presses Enter in the group-size field.</p><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class=\"answer\">The key-press event supplies information about the key action.</div></details>",
    "note": "用点击Search和按Enter说明事件既关联动作又可提供输入数据；按钮标签不是“这次事件”。可以演示按一下鼠标但不要写事件处理代码。CED列举程序启动也能生成事件，因此不要说所有事件都必须来自人工点击。本课只建立触发执行概念；事件驱动与顺序控制的正式比较、实现细节后续程序课继续。 先沿已有Search例子读动作、事件与执行，再让学生独立命名Enter情境；Enter题答案继续保持折叠。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Why the same click can give a different result",
    "tag": "INPUT & PRIOR STATE",
    "time": "52–55 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.C.4 · CRD-2.D.2",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">An app stores the number of completed tasks.</p><figure class=\"visual\" tabindex=\"0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two runs use the same Add-one click but start from counts 2 and 7, producing displays 3 and 8.\" viewBox=\"0 0 1200 245\" style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"15\" width=\"320\" height=\"98\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"35\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#225a83\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">Stored count</text><text x=\"282\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"45\" fill=\"#225a83\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><path d=\"M344 65L414 65\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"414,65 402.0,59.0 402.0,71.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"430\" y=\"15\" width=\"330\" height=\"98\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"595\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"28\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Same click</text><text x=\"595\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Complete one  →  +1</text><path d=\"M777 65L849 65\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"849,65 837.0,59.0 837.0,71.0\" fill=\"#225a83\"/><rect x=\"865\" y=\"15\" width=\"325\" height=\"98\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"889\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#225a83\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">Displayed</text><text x=\"1140\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"45\" fill=\"#225a83\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"133\" width=\"320\" height=\"98\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#28766f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"35\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#28766f\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">Stored count</text><text x=\"282\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"45\" fill=\"#28766f\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">7</text><path d=\"M344 183L414 183\" stroke=\"#28766f\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"414,183 402.0,177.0 402.0,189.0\" fill=\"#28766f\"/><rect x=\"430\" y=\"133\" width=\"330\" height=\"98\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#eef3f6\" stroke=\"#225a83\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"595\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"28\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Same click</text><text x=\"595\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#193148\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Complete one  →  +1</text><path d=\"M777 183L849 183\" stroke=\"#28766f\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"849,183 837.0,177.0 837.0,189.0\" fill=\"#28766f\"/><rect x=\"865\" y=\"133\" width=\"325\" height=\"98\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fcfcfa\" stroke=\"#28766f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"889\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#28766f\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\">Displayed</text><text x=\"1140\" y=\"201\" font-size=\"45\" fill=\"#28766f\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">8</text></svg></figure><p>Why does an identical click produce a different number?</p><details><summary>Show explanation</summary><div class=\"answer\">The output also depends on the program’s <strong>prior state</strong>: the stored count before the click.</div></details>",
    "note": "不要从“输入通常影响输出”推成“同一条当前输入永远同一输出”。本例完整解释差异来源是已有计数值，并非程序无规律或随机。state用“程序记住的当前值”解释即可，变量赋值与更新将在下一课展开。顺便提醒一项输入变化也不一定改变输出，例如两个不同组别都可能适合Room B。 两行只改变左侧已有值，中间操作保持相同。先请学生用箭头解释两条运行路径，再展开已有状态的解释。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Choose the purpose",
    "tag": "ORIGINAL AP-STYLE PRACTICE",
    "time": "55–59 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.A · Skill 1.A",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">An app converts a reader’s selected text into speech.</p><p>Which statement best describes its purpose?</p><div class=\"options\"><p>A. It receives selected text.</p><p>B. It produces an audio signal.</p><p>C. It helps users access written material by listening.</p><p>D. It uses program instructions.</p></div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class=\"answer\"><strong>C.</strong> It explains the user goal. A and B describe input/output; D identifies an implementation feature.</div></details>",
    "note": "独立选择30秒，然后要求学生为另外三个选项贴input/output/program feature标签。C不是因为句子最长，而是它解释创新为什么有用。不要限定只有视障读者可以使用，通勤者、语言学习者等也可能受益；目的表述可以适当广泛，但要与题干功能对应。此题是原创AP风格练习，不标真题。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Select exactly two inputs",
    "tag": "ORIGINAL AP-STYLE PRACTICE",
    "time": "59–63 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.C · CRD-2.D",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">A translation program reads a photo and a chosen target language, then displays translated text.</p><p>Which <strong>TWO</strong> are inputs to this program?</p><div class=\"options\"><p>A. The photo data</p><p>B. The translated text it displays</p><p>C. The selected target language</p><p>D. The program’s instructions</p></div><details><summary>Show both answers</summary><div class=\"answer\"><strong>A and C.</strong> B is output; D is the program that processes the supplied data.</div></details>",
    "note": "提醒必须选恰好两项，先判断每个选项再作答。照片是输入数据，不必是键盘文字。程序指令本身也以位存储，但题目划定的翻译程序中，它们负责处理，不是本次翻译请求提供的输入材料。不要引出编译器“代码也可作为另一程序输入”的例外，若学生主动问可肯定并指出边界不同。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Start with people, not a feature list",
    "tag": "UNDERSTAND THE USER",
    "time": "63–67 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.F.1–3 introduction",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">Before designing the room finder, investigate:</p><ol><li>Who needs to find a room?</li><li>What makes a room suitable for that person?</li><li>What constraints could prevent them using the result?</li></ol><p>Suggest one useful interview question.</p><details><summary>Show an example</summary><div class=\"answer\">“Tell me about the last time you struggled to find a study room. What made the search difficult?”</div></details>",
    "note": "不要代替用户想当然地列二十项功能。提问最好收集经历与约束，少问“你喜欢我们的好点子吗”。可提及轮椅通行、噪声需求、设备屏幕和开放时间，但不要假定群体所有成员需求一致。结对活动中一人扮演用户只能产生初步反馈，不能代替真实调查。对齐F.1–3为预习，不把一次访谈等同完整开发流程。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Make success observable",
    "tag": "SUCCESS CRITERIA",
    "time": "67–71 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.F.4 · CRD-2.J introduction",
    "html": "<div class=\"columns\"><div><h3>Too vague</h3><p>“The app should be good and easy.”</p></div><div><h3>Checkable requirement</h3><p>For a group of 4, show every available room with at least 4 seats.</p></div></div><p>With our room table, what result would demonstrate this requirement?</p><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class=\"answer\"><strong>Only Room B.</strong> Room A has too few seats; Room C is unavailable.</div></details>",
    "note": "成功标准应把要求转为可观察结果。这里不用宽泛“用户觉得好”当作程序正确性证据；但可用真实用户任务完成情况评估易用性。教学生区分检查一次样例与证明所有情况正确：Room B例子只是一个测试。提醒真正的程序还要处理不同组大小和无匹配结果，本课设计时至少考虑一项变化。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Design a room finder on paper",
    "tag": "PAIR DESIGN · 6 MINUTES",
    "time": "71–77 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.A · CRD-2.C · CRD-2.D · CRD-2.F",
    "html": "<p class=\"lead\">One designer + one user. Swap roles halfway.</p><ol><li>Write a purpose naming the user and their goal.</li><li>Sketch one screen. Label input data and output data.</li><li>Describe the processing in plain English.</li><li>Write one input case and its expected result.</li></ol><details><summary>Show a possible design</summary><div class=\"answer\">Example: group size 4 + room table → keep available rooms with enough seats → display Room B. Purpose: help study groups find suitable space.</div></details>",
    "note": "先1分钟访谈用户需求，再2分钟画图并注明数据方向；3分钟时交换角色，后半完成处理规则和一个检查案例。屏幕不要求美观，信息流清楚更重要。巡堂看四件证据：用户目标、实际数据而非设备名、至少一个处理动作、可核对的预期结果。只有明确需要才增加一个约束，如安静区域；不要不断加功能导致无法完成。答案在学生产出后再展示。"
  },
  {
    "title": "Try to break the design, then revise it",
    "tag": "PEER REVIEW · 5 MINUTES",
    "time": "77–82 min",
    "code": "CRD-2.B.3 · CRD-2.E.3 preview",
